{"name":"Crème Pâtissière","hex":"#fdd77a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crème pâtissière","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Confectioner's cream, pastry cream."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cr%C3%A8me_p%C3%A2tissi%C3%A8re"}],"entries":[{"title":"Custard","blocks":[{"text":"Custard is a variety of culinary preparations based on sweetened milk, cheese, or cream cooked with egg or egg yolk to thicken it, and sometimes also flour, corn starch, or gelatin. Depending on the recipe, custard may vary in consistency from a thin pouring sauce to the thick pastry cream used to fill éclairs. The most common custards are used in custard desserts or dessert sauces and typically include sugar and vanilla; however, savory custards are also found, e.g., in quiche."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Custard.jpg/330px-Custard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Custard","wikidata":"Q625825"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Dessertcustard.jpg/500px-Dessertcustard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Dessertcustard.jpg/500px-Dessertcustard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A formal custard preparation, garnished with raspberries","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADessertcustard.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Pastry_cream.jpg/500px-Pastry_cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Pastry_cream.jpg/1280px-Pastry_cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Pastry_cream.jpg/500p